<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Vladislav Janeček
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

The entitlements macos/Makefile signs into malachi-mcp alone. The bridge
reads the text of PDF attachments with PDFium compiled to WebAssembly,
which wazero translates to native code in memory it maps writable and
then executable, without MAP_JIT; under the hardened runtime of a
Developer ID build the kernel kills the process at the first PDF unless
this entitlement allows unsigned executable memory (allow-jit alone does
not). The worker that parses documents is malachi-mcp itself started
again as a child process, so it runs under this signature too. The app,
malachid and malachi-keychain run no such code and get none of it.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
